A pleading must give particulars of any of the following matters that are included in the pleading:
(a) breach of trust;
(b) fraud;

*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 13.7 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. August 14, 2010)]*

(1) A pleading may include all or any of the following:
(a) alternative claims or defences;
(b) a statement of a point of law, and if so, the facts that make the point of law applicable;
(c) a matter that arose after the commencement document was filed.
(2) A general or other remedy claimed by a party need not be claimed in a pleading.

*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 13.8 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. August 14, 2010)]*

